{"pack": "m2ui", "voice": "girl", "speaker": {"af_heart": 1.0}, "audio": "m2ui-20261117b.mp4", "model": "Kokoro-82M v1.0 (Apache 2.0) via kokoro-onnx (MIT); misaki phonemizer (Apache 2.0)", "gap": 0.45, "clips": {"Chapter 3 complete! Talk to Mo at the old dock, east of the lighthouse.": [0.0, 4.404], "Mayor Bea is waiting for you on the beach. Go and say hello!": [4.854, 3.487], "Say hello to Gus the clockmaker, on the beach.": [8.791, 2.655], "Explore Port Lumen and meet its people.": [11.895, 2.441], "Walk the Tidewalk to Port Lumen. It starts at the old dock, east of the lighthouse.": [14.787, 4.937], "You learned it all! Go see Gus in the Clock Tower. He heard something strange\u2026": [20.174, 4.191], "Someone is hiding up by the bells! Climb the ladder in the Clock Tower.": [24.815, 3.913], "Chapter 6 complete! Explore Port Lumen as much as you like.": [29.178, 3.913], "Help Rafi count his fish at the fish market. Count hundreds, tens and ones.": [33.541, 4.639], "Talk to Mayor Bea in the Town Hall: she has big news!": [38.63, 3.124], "Help Pedro count the people on his water taxi. He\u2019s on the Town Hall Plaza.": [42.204, 4.703], "Go see Gus in the Clock Tower. He found something!": [47.357, 3.081], "Chapter 4 complete! Now we know who sells the pages: the Crumb Crew!": [50.888, 4.255], "Chapter 5: why did the big clock stop?": [55.593, 2.612], "Chapter 5 complete! Someone took the Bell Gear to keep the bells quiet\u2026": [58.655, 4.468], "Chapter 6: who is hiding near the bells?": [63.573, 2.484], "The clock hand starts on 20. It jumps 3 tens to the right: 30, 40, 50.": [66.507, 5.62], "Count the hops: 1, 2, 3. Each hop is ten.": [72.577, 3.231], "It lands on 50! So 20 + 30 = 50.": [76.257, 3.615], "Now the hand goes back. It starts on 50 and jumps 2 tens to the LEFT: 40, 30.": [80.322, 5.94], "It lands on 30! Left means taking away: 50 \u2212 20 = 30.": [86.712, 5.108], "The hand can start between the marks, too. Start on 34 and jump 2 tens to the right: 44, 54.": [92.27, 7.241], "It lands on 54. Only the tens changed; the ones stay 4! So 34 + 20 = 54.": [99.961, 7.433], "Say hello to Mayor Bea in the Town Hall.": [107.845, 2.335], "Help Ms. Reyes read the new words on the Market Street signs!": [110.629, 3.465], "Lucy\u2019s robot fell apart on the Canal Walk. Help her build a new one!": [114.545, 4.276], "Help Captain Lin fill in her harbor book. She is on Museum Road.": [119.271, 3.785], "Walk the Tidewalk to Port Lumen! Start at the old dock, east of the lighthouse.": [123.506, 4.596], "Walk to the end of the old dock, to the right. The Tidewalk starts there!": [128.552, 4.063], "Cross the Tidewalk! Mina is at the first rope bridge. Win her challenge.": [133.065, 4.447], "Cadet Jo guards the second rope bridge. Win the challenge to reach Port Lumen!": [137.961, 4.873], "Keep walking east. Port Lumen\u2019s beach is just ahead!": [143.285, 3.295], "Ruby is by the broken taxi dock at the harbor. Help her fix it!": [147.029, 4.084], "You have 5 planks! Stand by the Harbor taxi stop. Press A to lay each one.": [151.563, 4.703], "Leo is waiting by the Clock Tower. Help put the loose gears back!": [156.716, 3.892], "You have 5 gears! Go into the Clock Tower. Press A by the big wheels.": [161.058, 4.127], "One question for each thing you learned on Market Street. Each right answer gives you a plank!": [165.635, 5.257], "You have all the planks! Go to the Harbor taxi stop. Press A to build the dock.": [171.342, 4.425], "One question for each thing you learned on the Canal Walk. Each right answer gives you a gear!": [176.217, 5.279], "You have all the gears! Go into the Clock Tower and press A by the big wheels.": [181.946, 4.297], "Port Lumen stamps:": [186.693, 1.353], "Still to visit in Port Lumen:": [188.497, 1.908], "Find the people with a !": [190.855, 1.567], "Port Lumen": [192.871, 1.076], "the Tidewalk": [194.397, 1.161], "A young otter with a red scarf steps out. {otter} jumps in front of you, fur up, with a little growl.": [196.009, 6.047], "Brioche stops. For a moment he just looks at {otter}.": [202.505, 3.316], "Hey, {otter} keeps looking into the water. Otters are great divers!": [206.271, 4.191], "Now {otter} can dive! Look for bubbles in the water near the shore.": [210.912, 3.977], "Brioche looks at {otter} one more time. He opens his mouth\u2026 then shuts it and runs off after the crew.": [215.339, 6.239], "Rafi has planks at the fish market.": [222.028, 2.143], "Learn with the people of Market Street, then come back!": [224.621, 3.103], "Gus says the storm knocked gears loose in the Clock Tower.": [228.173, 3.209], "Learn with the Canal Walk people!": [231.833, 1.929], "Look, {name}! The tide went out! Now there is a path of sand across the sea!": [234.212, 3.892], "This is the Tidewalk. It goes all the way to Port Lumen. That's the city on Marlo's sea chart.": [238.554, 5.705], "Explorers come here at low tide. Two of them guard the rope bridges: win their challenge to cross!": [244.709, 5.961], "Their challenges review what we learned on the island. Don\u2019t worry: if you miss, you get help and try again.": [251.121, 6.303], "THE TIDEWALK. Port Lumen \u2192 this way. Lighthouse Island \u2190 back across the dock. Walk only at low tide!": [257.873, 7.327], "THE TIDEWALK. Port Lumen, Old Town beach \u2192 right here. Lighthouse Island \u2190 across the sand and the bridges.": [265.65, 7.647], "A tide pool! When the tide goes out, sea water stays behind in the low places.": [273.747, 4.937], "Little animals wait in the pools until the sea comes back. Look, but leave them in their home.": [279.134, 5.428], "A tiny lighthouse on Little Light islet. At night it blinks, so boats don't hit the hidden sand.": [285.012, 5.833], "Gulls are resting on Gull islet. Shh\u2026 let them sleep!": [291.295, 3.913], "Halt, explorer! I\u2019m Mina. I watch the sea birds of the Tidewalk with my binoculars.": [295.659, 5.428], "This rope bridge is mine to guard. To cross, win my review challenge!": [301.537, 4.511], "It has a bit of all you learned on the island!": [306.497, 2.356], "Yes, let\u2019s play!. Not now..": [309.303, 1.78], "The bridge is open, {name}! Want to play again, just for fun?": [311.533, 3.103], "You remember so much! Here is a Tidewalk sticker for your notebook. The bridge is open!": [315.086, 5.087], "Hey, explorer! I\u2019m Milo. My kite flies best on the sandbars!": [320.623, 4.169], "Want a math challenge? Adding and taking away, up to 20. It\u2019s just for fun, you can say no!": [325.242, 6.025], "My kite is still up! Another math challenge?": [331.717, 2.719], "Wow, you\u2019re quick! Take a Tidewalk sticker!": [334.886, 2.335], "Hello, dear. I\u2019m Grandma Opal. I paint the tide pools while the sea is away.": [337.671, 5.023], "Do you like stories and words? Try my reading challenge. Only if you want to!": [343.143, 4.703], "Back for more words, dear? Another reading challenge?": [348.296, 3.039], "What a fine reader! Here is a Tidewalk sticker. I painted it myself.": [351.785, 4.212], "Shh\u2026 a crab! Oh, hi! I\u2019m Finn. I look for animals in the tide pools.": [356.447, 5.108], "Want a challenge about science and maps? Land and water, nature, and places! You can say no.": [362.005, 5.983], "Found anything in the pools? Want another science and maps challenge?": [368.437, 3.785], "You know your land and water! Here is a Tidewalk sticker!": [372.673, 3.188], "Ahoy! I\u2019m Cadet Jo of the coast watch. I keep the Tidewalk safe.": [376.311, 4.063], "To cross my bridge, show me what you learned on the island. Story problems too: first to 5 points!": [380.823, 6.281], "Miss on your first try and I get a point. Ready?": [387.555, 3.017], "The way to Port Lumen is open, {name}! Want to play again?": [391.022, 3.017], "Well done, explorer! Here is a Tidewalk sticker. The bridge is open: Port Lumen is just ahead!": [394.489, 5.919], "THE TIDEWALK. Low tide! Port Lumen \u2192 across the sand and the rope bridges.": [400.858, 5.108], "THE OLD DOCK. At high tide there is only sea here. At low tide\u2026 who knows?": [406.416, 4.575], "THE TIDEWALK. Lighthouse Island \u2190 across the sand and the rope bridges. Walk only at low tide!": [411.441, 6.644], "{name}, you beat all five Tidewalk explorers!": [418.535, 2.42], "That\u2019s the gold Tidewalk sticker! Look for it in your notebook, next to your treasures.": [421.405, 4.553], "The X isn't here anyway. Look: it's on an island far to the southeast. We'll find it first! Come on, crew!": [426.408, 6.516], "The old sea map is back in its case. The X is far to the southeast\u2026": [433.374, 4.34], "Look at that X\u2026 on an island far to the southeast. I wonder what's there.": [438.164, 4.297], "Gus (in the Clock Tower)": [442.911, 1.588], "Gus in the Clock Tower": [444.949, 1.567], "Mayor Bea (in the Town Hall)": [446.966, 1.716], "Mayor Bea in the Town Hall": [449.132, 1.567], "Pedro (by the Town Hall Plaza)": [451.149, 2.121], "Pedro by the Town Hall Plaza": [453.72, 2.015], "Captain Lin (in the Harbor Office)": [456.185, 2.143], "Captain Lin in the Harbor Office": [458.777, 2.036], "Rafi (at the fish market by the harbor)": [461.263, 2.399], "Rafi at the fish market by the harbor": [464.112, 2.271], "Coco (in the Ice Cream Parlor)": [466.833, 2.036], "Coco in the Ice Cream Parlor": [469.319, 1.951], "Pepper (in the Galleria)": [471.719, 1.481], "Pepper in the Galleria": [473.651, 1.396], "Mr. Fitz (in the Galleria)": [475.497, 1.823], "Mr. Fitz in the Galleria": [477.769, 1.673], "Dr. Kai (in the City Aquarium)": [479.893, 2.271], "Dr. Kai in the City Aquarium": [482.613, 2.185], "Ms. Reyes (in the City Library)": [485.249, 2.1], "Ms. Reyes in the City Library": [487.799, 2.036], "Dr. Amara (in the Museum)": [490.285, 2.079], "Dr. Amara in the Museum": [492.813, 1.972], "Olive (in the greenhouse, City Park)": [495.235, 2.335], "Olive in the greenhouse, City Park": [498.02, 2.185], "Mr. Bloom (on Market Street)": [500.655